{"criterion": "reproduction", "verdicts": [{"finding_id": "standalone-review:code-reviewer-1", "verdict": "upheld", "reasoning": "Concrete trigger exists: `/(^|\\/)(docs?|README)|\\.(md|mdx|txt)$/.test('docker-compose.yml')` matches via `^` + `doc` (the `s` is optional and nothing anchors the end), so a scope of only `docker-compose.yml`/`docker/Dockerfile` (derived by `deriveChangedPaths` in `startStandaloneFacade`, /home/peterstorm/dev/claude-plugins/loom/engine/src/handlers/helpers/programs/standalone.ts:26-35) yields docsOnly=true with sourceOrTestChanged=false, which passes the parse boundary at engine/src/core/standalone-review.ts:262 and then drops silent-failure-hunter (gated on `!metadata.docsOnly`, line 293) and adds comment-analyzer (line 298); for `.ts` paths like `src/docker/build.ts` the same match instead makes docsOnly && sourceOrTestChanged true and hard-fails the run at line 262-263, so every reproduction path ends in wrong behavior."}, {"finding_id": "standalone-review:silent-failure-hunter-1", "verdict": "upheld", "reasoning": "Reproducible from a registration whose variant is already matched but whose input is invalid, e.g. `{schemaVersion:1,kind:'remediation',input:{sourceRunsRoot:'',sourceRun:'x',supportPaths:[]}}`: helpers.ts:418-421 returns bare null, so `resumeOperation` (engine/src/handlers/helpers/orchestration.ts:715-726) falls through to the panel parser and reports the generic 'registered orchestration program is malformed' instead of parseRemediationStartInput's message, and an invalid-but-present wave-gate registration makes restartOperation (line 645-648) report 'restart currently requires a registered Wave Gate run' — a demonstrably wrong diagnostic for a run that IS a wave-gate run."}]}